Method Resolution Order — The Activity Series
Equivalent
A strict, fixed, checkable displacement ranking — same job, different table
The Activity Series doesn't describe attraction, it predicts EVICTION — put a higher-ranked element
near a lower-ranked one's compound, and the higher one displaces it. MRO does exactly this job for
method lookup: a strict, computed-once ordering that decides which class's version of a method displaces
another's, every time, no exceptions.
Mechanism
Python computes MRO via C3 linearization the moment a class is defined. The result is a fixed list
— checkable with ClassName.__mro__ — that governs every subsequent method lookup on that
class, the same way the Activity Series, once memorized, governs every displacement reaction that
follows it.
READING THE RANKING
A ranks above B in C's MRO, the same way Zinc ranks above Copper in the Reactivity Series. A's
greet() displaces B's — not because A's version is better, but purely because of fixed positional rank.
