ON WATER — TWO CORRECT READINGS, NOT A CONFLICT
Water in the chemistry book plays two separate, equally correct roles: it is THE textbook
Amphoteric substance (autoionization), and separately it is the byproduct sitting on the right side
of Acid + Base = Salt + Water. Neither reading cancels the other. In this Python table, the byproduct
reading maps to console output / logs — the ambient thing produced by a reaction running — while
the amphoteric reading earns its own seat in the bucket above, on its own chemical merits.
The reaction itself, restated in this book's own terms: CSV + report_template.html (+ generator script) = rendered student page
(Salt) + console output (byproduct, water's other role). The generator is the Acid; the CSV and template are both Bases; what
drops out afterward no longer needs the script that made it.
